("Go away," Helena said. Her voice was a whisper, but it was steady.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 445 Tm
("Helena, I") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 425 Tm
("Go away or I'll scream. I'll scream and the whole street will know a German officer is at a Polish woman's door, and you can explain that to whoever you need to explain it to.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 405 Tm
(Silence. A long, stretching silence. She could hear him breathing on the other side of the wood. She could hear the faint creak of leather as he shifted his weight.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 385 Tm
(Then: "The child. Is thathow old is she?") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 365 Tm
(Helena closed her eyes.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 345 Tm
("She's nine.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 325 Tm
(Another silence.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 305 Tm
("I need to know," he said, and his voice had changedlower now, rougher, as though something in his throat had tightened. "Her father. Helena, who is") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 285 Tm
("You have no right. You lost every right the day you" She stopped. Swallowed. "Go away.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 265 Tm
(More silence. Then footsteps, receding. Down the stairs. A door opening and closing below.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 245 Tm
(Helena slid down the wall until she was sitting on the floor, Marysia still clutched to her chest. She held the girl and she rocked her, back and forth, and she did not cry. She had made a vow ten years ago that she would not cry for Jochen von Brandt, and she would keep that vow until the day she died, even if keeping it burned her from the inside out like a coal swallowed whole.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 225 Tm
("Mama?" Marysia's voice was small, muffled by the coat. "Who was that man?") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 205 Tm
(Helena pressed her lips together. The truth sat on her tongue, sharp and poisonous. That man is your father. That man is the reason you exist. That man is the reason I lie awake at night counting the ways the world could end.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 185 Tm
("No one," she said. "No one you need to know.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 165 Tm
(Outside, the snow continued to fall, covering the city in white, covering everything in white, as though it mightmight, if the world were merciful, which it was notcover everything and make it new.) Tj
