1 0 0 1 50 505 Tm
("I was twenty-one. And I left.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 485 Tm
(The silence that followed was absolute. Jochen looked at her, and she looked at him, and between them lay ten years of unspoken thingsthe letters he had never sent, the ring she had left on the nightstand, the child who was walking down a corridor in a German administrative building, carrying the blood of both of them in her veins like a secret encoded in her cells.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 465 Tm
