(During those weeks, the occupation pressed against the city with a new and particular cruelty. February gave way to a cold that was not merely meteorological but politicala coldness that seeped from the walls of the Gestapo headquarters, from the barracks on Aleja Szucha, from the processing centers where civilians were sorted like parcels and dispatched to destinations that were, for the most part, final. The ghetto was being liquidatedblock by block, family by familyand the sounds of the liquidation carried across the city like the distant thunder of a storm that was approaching but had not yet arrived.) Tj
