1 0 0 1 50 155 Tm
(The third way was this: she would warn Jochen. She would tell him about the sweepthe planned operation in Mokotow that Marek had mentioned. She would give him the information that would allow him to protect himself, to avoid being in a position where his name would be connected to anything that went wrong. And in doing so, she would give him something he could usenot intelligence that would harm Germany, but information that would keep him safe. It was a compromise. It was, by the strict standards of the resistance, inadequate. But it was all she could give without crossing a line she was not willing to cross.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 135 Tm
(Her father died in 1942. It was the winter of the Great Actionthe mass deportation from Warsaw that sent three hundred thousand Jews to Treblinka in the space of two months. Helena's father was not Jewish, but he was a professor, and the Germans had a particular hatred for professors. They understood, in the way that all tyrants understand, that the people who teach are the people who remember, and that memory is the enemy of erasure.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 115 Tm
