(She waited three weeks. She went back to the Pawiak every three days. Each time, the same answer: not here, transferred, processing. On the fourth visit, the clerka different clerk, a younger one, with the uncertain eyes of someone who had not yet been entirely dehumanized by the workleaned across the counter and said, in a voice barely above a whisper: "Your father is dead. He was executed at Palmiry on the twentieth of January. His body is in the forest. Do not come back here. They are watching you.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 525 Tm
(Helena walked out of the Pawiak and into the street and she did not cry. She walked home. She told her mother. Her mothera woman who had been strong for thirty years of marriage, who had raised a daughter, who had kept a household through hyperinflation and depression and war, who had never, in all that time, shown weaknessher mother collapsed. Not dramatically. Not with a cry or a faint. She simply sat down in her chair and she did not get up again. She stopped eating. She stopped speaking. She looked at the wall with the steady, vacant gaze of a person who has decided, with the quiet finality of the very old, that the world is no longer a place worth inhabiting.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 505 Tm
