("Go.") Tj
1 0 0 1 50 125 Tm
(His voice was not a plea. It was a commandthe voice of an officer, the voice of a man who has made a decision and will not be dissuaded from it. Helena felt the weight of the decision in the air between thema decision that was not new, that had been building since the day he saw her in the street, since the day he signed the release, since the day he chose her over his family and now, in a sewer under a burning city, was choosing her one final time.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 105 Tm
(She turned. She ran. She ran through the water with Marysia on her back, her boots splashing, her breath coming in ragged gasps, the darkness pressing against her like a physical thing. Behind her, she heard the German patrol's flashlight beam sweep the tunnel, heard a shouted command, heard the sound of impactmetal on metal, or metal on flesh, she couldn't telland then the sound of shouting and splashing and the chaos of violence in a confined space.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 85 Tm
(She did not look back.) Tj
1 0 0 1 50 65 Tm
(She reached the junction. She took the left fork. She climbed the iron ladder to a manhole that opened onto a street in Pragathe Praga side of the river, where the Germans had not yet reached, where the city was still Polish, where the sky was the color of smoke but was, nonetheless, a sky that belonged to them.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
